---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Case Studies | Product Thinking & Solutions Engineering">
<header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Selected work / Product to execution</span><h1>Stay curious.<br/><span class="accent">Keep building.</span></h1><p>Each case study explores the business problem, the choices behind the solution, and the technical work needed to make an impact. Additional product, cloud architecture, and AI projects will be added here.</p></header>
<section class="section case-study" id="case-study" aria-labelledby="case-heading">
  <div class="section-row">
    <span class="eyebrow">01 / Selected case study</span>
    <div class="case-main">
      <div class="case-intro">
        <div><span class="case-kicker">Valor Compounding Pharmacy · Customer operations</span><h2 id="case-heading">Designing a fairer performance measurement approach.</h2>
          <p class="case-summary">Rethinking how customer-care performance is understood across prescription processing, phone interactions, service issues, and follow-ups—beyond a single output metric.</p></div>
        <div class="case-chips"><span>Product discovery</span><span>Metrics design</span><span>Qlik reporting</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="case-workspace" data-case-tabs>
        <div class="case-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the performance measurement case study">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-problem" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="case-panel-problem" tabindex="0" data-case-tab="problem"><span>01</span> Problem</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-opportunity" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-opportunity" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="opportunity"><span>02</span> Opportunity</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-solution" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-solution" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="solution"><span>03</span> Solution</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-technical" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-technical" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="technical"><span>04</span> Technical approach</button>
        </div>
        <div class="case-panels">
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-problem" aria-labelledby="case-tab-problem" data-case-panel="problem" tabindex="0">
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">The customer problem</span>
            <h3>One metric couldn't tell the whole story.</h3>
            <p>Customer-care performance was primarily assessed by the number of prescriptions typed. However, the team also handled phone interactions, service issues, and follow-ups. A volume-only measure missed important parts of the work.</p>
            <div class="panel-takeaway"><strong>Core challenge</strong><span>Capture a more complete picture of contribution without reducing varied responsibilities to one number.</span></div>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-opportunity" aria-labelledby="case-tab-opportunity" data-case-panel="opportunity" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">The opportunity</span>
            <h3>Make performance more representative.</h3>
            <p>Define a framework that considers the work performed across Central Fill, Direct to Patient, and shared customer-care functions.</p>
            <div class="panel-takeaway"><strong>Intended stakeholder views</strong><span>Department, role, and individual levels—so each audience can understand performance in the appropriate context.</span></div>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-solution" aria-labelledby="case-tab-solution" data-case-panel="solution" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">Solution direction</span>
            <h3>Look beyond prescription counts.</h3>
            <ul><li>Understand the responsibilities of Central Fill, Direct to Patient, and shared customer-care roles.</li><li>Consider prescriptions, calls, service tickets, resolution times, and attendance as complementary signals.</li><li>Plan Qlik views that provide context rather than relying on a single productivity measure.</li></ul>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-technical" aria-labelledby="case-tab-technical" data-case-panel="technical" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">Technical foundation</span>
            <h3>Translate operational activity into useful views.</h3>
            <p>The proposed approach centered on business intelligence, KPI modeling, reporting design, and role-specific performance views using Qlik.</p>
            <div class="panel-takeaway"><strong>Evidence boundary</strong><span>The source documents an intended framework and deliverables. Verified deployment outcomes or impact percentages were not provided.</span></div>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="case-footer"><span class="case-status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Documented solution approach · Outcomes not independently verified</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Visual exploration</span><div><h2>Data visualization &amp; storytelling.</h2><p>My Tableau Public portfolio is a collection of interactive visual explorations and storytelling through data. It's one expression of how I make complex information easier to explore and understand.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/bhagyashri.patil" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Tableau Public ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://www.tableau.com/blog/featured-authors-back-school-edition" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tableau Featured Author ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Coming next</span><div><h2>Product, architecture, and AI work.</h2><p>Future case studies will cover product decisions, system architecture, technical trade-offs, AI experiments, and measurable outcomes as supporting material becomes available.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/patilbp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse GitHub ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="publications" class="section" aria-labelledby="publications-heading">
  <div class="section-row">
    <span class="eyebrow">04 / Publications</span>
    <div><h2 id="publications-heading">Published work.</h2><p>Two earlier publications on assistive technology. Included here as part of my technical background, rather than as a separate research-focused career path.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="publication-grid">
    <article class="publication">
      <span class="eyebrow">Publication / 2016</span>
      <h3>Camera-Based Assistive Text and Product Label Reading for Blind Person</h3>
      <p>International Journal of Innovative Research and Creative Technology (IJIRCT).</p>
      <a href="https://www.ijirct.org/papers/IJIRCT1601003.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View publication ↗</a>
    </article>
    <article class="publication">
      <span class="eyebrow">Publication / 2015</span>
      <h3>Camera-Based Assistive Text and Product Label Reading for Blind Person</h3>
      <p>International Engineering Research Journal (IERJ).</p>
      <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Bhagyashri-Patil-6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ResearchGate profile ↗</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.case-main{min-width:0}
.case-intro{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.case-intro>div:first-child{flex:1 1 550px;min-width:0}
.case-kicker,.panel-eyebrow{font-size:.74rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#536bd0}
.case-main h2{max-width:880px;margin:12px 0 15px}
.case-summary{max-width:820px;margin:0;color:#60718a;font-size:1rem}
.case-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-self:flex-start}
.case-chips span{white-space:nowrap;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:750;color:#4961aa;padding:8px 10px;background:#edf2ff;border:1px solid #e1e9fb;border-radius:999px}
.case-workspace{border:1px solid #dfe7f2;border-radius:18px;background:#fff;margin-top:26px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 8px 30px #1c376408}
.case-tabs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:0;background:#f5f8fe;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7f2}
.case-tabs button{border:0;border-bottom:3px solid transparent;padding:17px 10px 14px;background:transparent;color:#697994;font:750 .87rem "DM Sans",sans-serif;cursor:pointer;text-align:center;transition:background .15s,color .15s}
.case-tabs button span{color:#8494b5;font-weight:800;font-size:.7rem;margin-right:6px}
.case-tabs button[aria-selected="true"]{color:#253a6c;background:#fff;border-bottom-color:#4d6bdd}
.case-tabs button:hover{color:#284dad;background:#eef3fe}
.case-tabs button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #4c6ddc;outline-offset:-4px}
.case-panels{padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,36px);min-height:260px}
.case-panels [hidden]{display:none!important}
.case-panels h3{font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2vw,1.7rem);margin:10px 0 13px}
.case-panels p{max-width:850px;font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 18px}
.case-panels ul{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:11px;color:#59697f;font-size:.96rem;line-height:1.6}
.panel-takeaway{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 17px;border-left:3px solid #4c69d8;background:#f5f8ff;padding:13px 17px;border-radius:0 9px 9px 0;color:#50627d;font-size:.89rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:850px}
.panel-takeaway strong{color:#263b66;flex:0 0 auto}
.panel-takeaway span{flex:1 1 400px}
.case-footer{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;border-top:1px solid #e6ebf4;padding:12px clamp(22px,2.6vw,36px);color:#79879a;font-size:.75rem}
.case-status-dot{background:#8c9cba;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:100%;flex-shrink:0}
@media(max-width:650px){.case-tabs{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.case-tabs button{padding:12px 7px;font-size:.8rem}.case-panels{min-height:0}.case-chips{gap:6px}.case-footer{align-items:flex-start}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.case-tabs button{transition:none}}
</style>
<script>
  const initializeCaseTabs = () => {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-case-tabs]').forEach((workspace) => {
      if (workspace.hasAttribute('data-ready')) return;
      workspace.setAttribute('data-ready', 'true');
      const tabs = Array.from(workspace.querySelectorAll('[data-case-tab]'));
      const panels = Array.from(workspace.querySelectorAll('[data-case-panel]'));
      const activate = (tab, focus = false) => {
        const name = tab.getAttribute('data-case-tab');
        tabs.forEach((item) => {
          const active = item === tab;
          item.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(active));
          item.tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1;
        });
        panels.forEach(panel => { panel.hidden = panel.getAttribute('data-case-panel') !== name; });
        if (focus) tab.focus();
      };
      tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => activate(tab));
        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          let next = index;
          if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') next = (index + 1) % tabs.length;
          else if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') next = (index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
          else if (event.key === 'Home') next = 0;
          else if (event.key === 'End') next = tabs.length - 1;
          else return;
          event.preventDefault();
          activate(tabs[next], true);
        });
      });
    });
  };
  initializeCaseTabs();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initializeCaseTabs);
</script>

<style>.accent{color:#4667d4}</style>
<style>
.publication-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;margin-top:30px}
.publication{padding:28px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e1e8f2;border-radius:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.publication h3{margin:16px 0}
.publication p{flex:1}
.publication a{font-weight:800;font-size:.9rem;color:#4264cd}
.publication a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
@media(max-width:700px){.publication-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
